{
  "id": "09300_disuru",
  "headword": "ディスる",
  "reading": "でぃする",
  "part_of_speech": "godan verb",
  "gloss": "to diss; to disrespect; to badmouth",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to diss; to disrespect; to badmouth",
      "explanation": "To speak negatively about someone or show disrespect, often publicly or in a mocking way."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "09300_disuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "ディスられた。",
      "english": "I got dissed.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09300_disuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "SNSで{有名人|ゆうめいじん}をディスる。",
      "english": "To badmouth celebrities on social media.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09300_disuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{人|ひと}をディスるのはよくない。",
      "english": "It's not good to diss other people.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "ディスる comes from the English \"diss\" (short for \"disrespect\"), originally from hip-hop culture. It entered Japanese through rap and internet culture.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is slang primarily used by younger generations and on the internet. In formal contexts, use {批判|ひはん}する, {悪口|わるくち}を{言|い}う, or {馬鹿|ばか}にする.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～をディスる: to diss someone/something\n- ディスられる: to get dissed (passive)",
